    "difficultyReason": "Parts a to c are direct formula applications: square area, rectangle area and a right triangle with its legs given. Part d is the hardest essential demand. The student must link the similarity scale factor to the dimensions or area of B. They can scale the sides to 6 by 15 and multiply, or find A's area and multiply by 3². Either route is a short, routine two-step procedure, with the scale factor supplied and A's dimensions on the diagram. The only decision beyond direct recall is applying the scale factor to area, not just to length. This is more than the repeated one-step expansions in p44-q3, but less than the interpretive step in p45-q6.",
